Affected component: the application layer on the remote server (srv1, 10.5.0.4) — specifically the HTTP service. Mechanism: Inter-building network connectivity is intact (ICMP reachability from pc1/pc2/pc3 to 10.5.0.4 succeeds with 0% loss and low RTTs; the core/distribution FRR routers all have OSPF routes to 10.5.0.0/24). However, application connections to the server fail because no web service is listening on the expected ports. Our curl tests from multiple clients to http://10.5.0.4 immediately complete with no payload, and a direct curl with status output from pc2 returns failure. On srv1, netstat/ss show only DNS (tcp/udp 53) and loopback listeners; there is no TCP listener on 80/443. systemctl confirms apache2 
